=== §7 part 1 (RACE-01, RACE-02) done ===
=== RACE-01 correction (harness bug, not a contract bug) ===
Root cause: `cast send`'s shell exit code reflects "the tx was broadcast and a receipt was fetched",
NOT "the on-chain receipt status was success" -- when two conflicting transactions both pass
cast's pre-broadcast gas-estimation simulation (because, at each one's individual estimation
moment, the conflicting tx hadn't landed yet), cast happily broadcasts both and exits 0 for both,
even though exactly one reverts once actually mined. The original RACE-01 check only looked at
shell exit code and wrongly flagged "2 winners".
Verified via `cast receipt <tx2 hash>`: both transactions landed in the SAME block
(0x380f6d5d...), tx1 at index 3 (status 1, success), tx2 at index 4 (status 0, failed, gasUsed
56555, zero logs emitted -- consistent with a revert before InvoiceRegistered would have fired).
Real, deterministic outcome: exactly one of the two concurrently-submitted same-nonce
registrations landed; the other reverted cleanly on-chain. This is the CORRECT, expected
behavior -- the harness's status-field check was the bug, not the contract.
PASS  RACE-01  exactly one of two concurrent same-nonce registrations landed on-chain (tx1 status=1 in block 0x380f6d5d idx3, tx2 status=0 idx4, same block)
PASS  RACE-01b  the loser's tx (tx2) reverted with zero gas-used-for-logs and no InvoiceRegistered event, consistent with NonceNotSequential -- no stuck or ambiguous state
